{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-224279","model_call":18,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"reflective teaching\" \"why\" teachers (+ important benefits) (+ improve learning instruction))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"reflective teaching\" \"why\" teachers (+ important benefits) (+ improve learning instruction))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_1160365489#7_2582746970","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q554","rank":1,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_1160365489#7_2582746970\" , \"end_char\": 5158.000000 , \"headings\": \"Why Reflection Is Important In Teaching<cover>Why Reflection Is Important In Teaching Making Reflection Part Of Your Teaching Practice Reflection As A Strategy To Improve Social Equity Four Strategies For Reflective Teaching Build Community Create a cycle of reflection Choose a Purpose Use Open-Ended Probing Questions About The Author TeachThought Staff \" , \"segment\": \"A Model For 21st-Century Learning On another level, teachers </cover>are honestly confronting their biases and values in a way that strengthens their belief in an ability to create positive change in the lives of their students. According to Malcolm, a high school teacher, “Reflecting teaches us the importance of respect, and reflecting on your biases.” For Sky Hobbs, a high school teacher, “Reflection has allowed me to re-examine my ‘Why’ and reconnect with my students especially during this remote learning process.” We are finding that through reflection teachers build a sense of agency. As Devin said in one of our discussions, “I feel like we’re in the ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_1160365489#7_2582746970","rank":1,"relevance":3}]},"time":86},"model_calls":18,"document_judgments":14,"relevance_3":10,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
