{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-224279","model_call":23,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"teacher self-assessment\" (+ importance benefits) (+ improve effective) (+ instruction teaching) students)"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"teacher self-assessment\" (+ importance benefits) (+ improve effective) (+ instruction teaching) students)"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_1004064348#0_2084570869","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q558","rank":1,"snippet":"the same things in the same way, to teach the same concepts the same way, and to use the same exercises again and again. Guess what? If a teacher does the same things the same way he or she has always done them, the results are going to be the same that they have always been in the past. Some teachers are pleased with their results and have the attitude that they do not need to change any of their teaching practices. However, for those teachers that are overachievers, it is imperative that they reflect on what they taught, how they taught certain concepts, and how effective their <cover>teaching/instructional strategies were. Self-Assessment Leads to Improvement Once teachers begin the evaluation process, they will see in which areas they can improve. How can I make the concept of _______ stick in my students’ heads?\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"The Importance of Teacher Self-Assessment: </cover>The First Step in Implementing A Teacher Improvement Plan - BrightHub Education\" , \"url\": \"http://www.brighthubeducation.com/teaching-methods-tips/15761-importance-of-teacher-self-assessment/\" }"},"time":163},"model_calls":23,"document_judgments":17,"relevance_3":12,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
